    "DEFINITION OF AN ADJECTIVE\nAn adjective is a word that modifies (describes) a noun or pronoun.\n'The tall boy' — tall modifies boy.\n\nTYPES OF ADJECTIVES\n1. Descriptive: beautiful, large, red.\n2. Numeral: three books, first prize.\n3. Demonstrative: this, that, these, those (before a noun).\n4. Possessive: my, your, his, her, our, their.\n5. Interrogative: which, what, whose.\n\nDEGREES OF COMPARISON\n1. Positive: Basic form — tall, beautiful.\n2. Comparative: Comparing two things — taller, more beautiful.\n3. Superlative: Comparing three or more — tallest, most beautiful.\n\nIrregular forms: good→better→best; bad→worse→worst; many→more→most.",
