    "DEFINITION OF AN ADVERB\nAn adverb modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb. It answers: How? When? Where? How often? How much?\n\nTYPES OF ADVERBS\n1. Manner (How?): slowly, quickly, well, badly — 'She spoke softly.'\n2. Time (When?): now, yesterday, soon, already — 'He will arrive tomorrow.'\n3. Place (Where?): here, there, inside, nearby — 'Come here.'\n4. Frequency (How often?): always, usually, never — 'She always does her homework.'\n5. Degree (How much?): very, quite, almost, too — 'The test was extremely difficult.'\n\nFORMING ADVERBS\nAdd -ly to adjectives: quick→quickly; careful→carefully; happy→happily.",
