    "PREPOSITIONS\nA preposition shows relationship between a noun/pronoun and another word.\nCommon prepositions — Position: in, on, at, beside, between, under.\nDirection: to, into, through, across. Time: at, on, in, before, after.\n'The book is on the table.' (position)\n\nCONJUNCTIONS\nA conjunction joins words, phrases, or clauses.\n1. Coordinating (FANBOYS): for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so.\n   'He is tall, but she is short.'\n2. Subordinating: because, although, when, while, if, unless, since, until.\n   'She studied hard because she wanted to pass.'",
